Below is a brief mapping of the columns that matter for this task, why we need them, and typical conditions that will be applied in the queries that follow.

Relevant columns and potential usage
• olist_order_payments.order_id : primary key needed to JOIN with olist_order_items  
• olist_order_payments.payment_type : tells us the payment method used – we must count these  
• olist_order_items.order_id : JOIN key to link an order to the items (and therefore to the products bought)  
• olist_order_items.product_id : JOIN key to pull the product’s category  
• olist_products.product_id : JOIN key coming from items to get the category name  
• olist_products.product_category_name : the Brazilian‑Portuguese category we will aggregate on  
• product_category_name_translation.product_category_name_english : (optional) human‑readable English category  

Typical conditions / filters likely used later
• WHERE payment_type IS NOT NULL  
• GROUP BY product_category_name, payment_type  
• ORDER BY number_of_payments DESC  
• LIMIT 3   – after ranking to keep the top three categories  

Ten exploratory / stepping‑stone SQL queries
(Each query is limited to 20 rows and uses DISTINCT wherever it makes sense)

```sql
-- 1. Description: List every distinct payment type available.
SELECT DISTINCT payment_type
FROM olist_order_payments
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: List the first 20 distinct product categories (Portuguese names).
SELECT DISTINCT product_category_name
FROM olist_products
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Show the Portuguese‑to‑English category translation for the first 20 categories.
SELECT product_category_name, product_category_name_english
FROM product_category_name_translation
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Count total number of payments per payment_type (top 20).
SELECT payment_type,
       COUNT(*) AS num_payments
FROM olist_order_payments
GROUP BY payment_type
ORDER BY num_payments DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Pull 20 random rows linking a product to its category and the order it belonged to.
SELECT oi.order_id,
       oi.product_id,
       p.product_category_name
FROM olist_order_items AS oi
JOIN olist_products    AS p
  ON oi.product_id = p.product_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Join payments to items to see what payment_type was used for a given product_id.
SELECT op.order_id,
       op.payment_type,
       oi.product_id
FROM olist_order_payments AS op
JOIN olist_order_items   AS oi
  ON op.order_id = oi.order_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Show the raw counts of payments by (product_category_name, payment_type).
SELECT p.product_category_name,
       op.payment_type,
       COUNT(*) AS num_payments
FROM olist_order_payments AS op
JOIN olist_order_items   AS oi ON op.order_id = oi.order_id
JOIN olist_products      AS p  ON oi.product_id = p.product_id
GROUP BY p.product_category_name,
         op.payment_type
ORDER BY num_payments DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: For each category, find the most used payment_type and its count (window function).
SELECT product_category_name,
       payment_type,
       num_payments,
       ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
           PARTITION BY product_category_name
           ORDER BY num_payments DESC
       ) AS rn
FROM (
    SELECT p.product_category_name,
           op.payment_type,
           COUNT(*) AS num_payments
    FROM olist_order_payments AS op
    JOIN olist_order_items   AS oi ON op.order_id = oi.order_id
    JOIN olist_products      AS p  ON oi.product_id = p.product_id
    GROUP BY p.product_category_name,
             op.payment_type
) AS sub
WHERE rn = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Rank every category by how many payments its top payment_type registered.
WITH top_payment_per_category AS (
    SELECT product_category_name,
           payment_type,
           num_payments,
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
               PARTITION BY product_category_name
               ORDER BY num_payments DESC
           ) AS rn
    FROM (
        SELECT p.product_category_name,
               op.payment_type,
               COUNT(*) AS num_payments
        FROM olist_order_payments AS op
        JOIN olist_order_items   AS oi ON op.order_id = oi.order_id
        JOIN olist_products      AS p  ON oi.product_id = p.product_id
        GROUP BY p.product_category_name,
                 op.payment_type
    )
)
SELECT product_category_name,
       payment_type,
       num_payments
FROM top_payment_per_category
WHERE rn = 1
ORDER BY num_payments DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final step – return the TOP 3 product categories whose most common payment_type
--                  amassed the highest number of payments.
WITH top_payment_per_category AS (
    SELECT product_category_name,
           payment_type,
           COUNT(*) AS num_payments,
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
               PARTITION BY product_category_name
               ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC
           ) AS rn
    FROM olist_order_payments AS op
    JOIN olist_order_items   AS oi ON op.order_id = oi.order_id
    JOIN olist_products      AS p  ON oi.product_id = p.product_id
    GROUP BY product_category_name,
             payment_type
)
SELECT product_category_name,
       payment_type,
       num_payments
FROM top_payment_per_category
WHERE rn = 1               -- keep only the dominant payment_type for each category
ORDER BY num_payments DESC -- now rank the categories by that dominant count
LIMIT 3;
```

